rgin  1 0cm from the inferior margin and 0 9cm from the anterior margin  1 5cm from the lateral margin and 2 0cm from the medial margin  A firm area is identified on the posterolateral margin and is focally confluent with the mass  A representative section of this area is submitted in E  Two posterior margin sections are placed in B  anterior margin is in C  and representative section of the mass is in D  Additional sections of mass are placed in O Q  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast tissue close to post inferior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm yellow red firm fibrofatty piece of tissue  Specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a yellow lobulated cut surface with focal areas of pink white tissue and submitted entirely in F H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm yellow tan irregular firm fibrofatty piece of tissue  Tissue is inked in black  serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm firm nodule that is 0 2cm from the nearest inked margin  Entire lesion is taken and placed in I  The rest of the specimen is sectioned and submitted in R T  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional tissue  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm yellow firm irregular fibrofatty piece of tissue with a suture present  With the stitch in the superior position  the superior margin is inked in black  Specimen is serially sectioned to reveal yellow lobulated fatty cut surface with focal areas of pink tan tissue  Specimen is submitted in entirety in J N  Section code  A  sentinel lymph node  B  posterior margin x2  C  anterior margin  D  representative section of mass  E  suspicious area posterior lateral of margin  F H left breast posterior inferior margin  I  firm area from  left breast mass   J N additio