Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 MAY 94 ACCESSIONED ON  04 MAY 94 at 16 04 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass with fine needle aspiration positive for malignancy  needs ER and PR                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  97    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE ANTERIOR SURGICAL RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3    CRIBRIFORM TYPE  3  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  MULTIFOCAL  4  FIBROCYSTIC DISEASE WITH DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  APOCRINE CHANGE AND MICROCYSTS  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   ELEVEN OF ELEVEN LYMPH NODES ARE NEGATIVE FOR MALIGNANCY   ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE   ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE IS NEGATIVE FOR MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD Signed On  09 MAY 94 at 17 57                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 MAY 94 at 14 48     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm breast biopsy with a short stitch marking superior and a long stitch marking lateral  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a hard  gritty  white brown stellate shaped mass  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm  located 0 5cm from the anterior resection margin closest  5 0cm from the superior resection margin  7 0cm from the lateral resection margin  3 5cm from the medial resection margin  and 1 5cm from the deep resection margin  The remainder of the specimen is noted for large areas of normal appearing soft tan breast parenchyma and adipose tissue  SECTION CODE  A  superior resection margin  en face B  lateral resection margin  en face C  inferior resection margin  en face D  medial resection margin  en face E  deep resection margin  radial F  tumor and anterior resection margin  closest G  section of tumor  disregard inked margin  artifact H  deep resection margin and cystic area  adjacent to tumor I  tumor and anterior resection margin J  representative normal breast  Received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm mass of adipose tissue and lymph nodes  Lymph nodes  11  measuring up to 3 0cm in greatest dimension are dissected and submitted in cassettes K through Q  Also received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  addition axillary tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tissue with one lymph node  submitted in R  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   BREAST LEFT   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  James Kirby  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST MASS PART B  LEFT AXILLA TISSUE PART C  LEFT AXILLA CONTENTS   report_end  , Micro.
