nked black  the superior margin is inked blue  the medial margin is inked green  and the lateral margin is inked yellow  The localization wire traverses the specimen in the anterior to posterior axis  and the specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior to reveal a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm region of hemorrhage  with surrounding dense nodular gray white fibrous tissue in the central portion  The dense fibrous tissue approximates to REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 8cm and abuts the superomedial margin  The area comes to 1 5cm of the lateral  1 8cm of the inferior  1 4cm of the anterior  and 1 8cm of the posterior margins  The remaining tissue is dense  gray white  and fibrous with focal adjacent unremarkable fatty tissue  Representative sections are submitted from anterior to posterior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the anterior margin en face as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the posterior margin radially sectioned as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the hemorrhagic focus with surrounding dense gray white fibrous tissue as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   additional representative sections of fibrous parenchyma from anterior to posterior  Received are 2 additional containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  posterior margin left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of tan red fibrofatty tissue  with no orientation  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable tan yellow fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast inferior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm portion of tan red fibrofatty tissue  with a black stitch along 1 aspect indicating the new margin  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal focal hemorrhage and dense gray white fibrous tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on Sunday REMOVED_MONTH 04   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03 16 41PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  Additional immunohistochemistry results A small epithelial proliferation near the inferior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   is consistent with a benign lobule with prominent myoepithelium and basement membrane  immunostains for calponin  smooth muscle myosin heavy chain  p63  and cytokeratin support the interpretation  Addendum  1 by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 08   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 35 42PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Left   Excision PART B  Breast  Left posterior Margin   Excision PART C  Breast  Left inferior Margin   Excision  report_end  , Micro.
