Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 49 CLINICAL DATA  Previous ductal cell cancer right breast in  REMOVED_CASE_ID                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  ABOUT 70   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  ABOUT 30    SEE NOTE  NOTE  Tumor focally invades the deep dermis of the overlying skin  Tumor is focally present within a few cell diameters of the inked margin  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 58                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE  6   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor specimen consists  predominantly of an in situ disease  The 6  relects invasive tumor only  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 16     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Positive 132 fm mg cytosolic protein progesterone receptor  Not determined Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 AUG 93 at 11 59 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  Right breast  is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm tan slightly firm piece of tissue that has been previously cut  A REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm unremarkable skin ellipse partially covers the specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  ill defined  tan  stellate  firm lesion that underlies the skin and abuts an inked resection margin  A representative piece of this lesion is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved  A piece is sent for EM and BRDU  The entire specimen is submitted as A through E  Resident  James Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST   INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Gross.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 MAY 93 ACCESSIONED ON  12 MAY 93 at 15 40 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY   INFILTRATING AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor grows with an unusual pattern that makes it difficult to determine the proportions of in situ and invasive carcinoma  Blood vessel or lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The tumor shows staining for chromogranin and synaptophysin  which indicates neuroendocrine differentiation  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 MAY 93 at 16 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 MAY 93 at 13 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  Sectioning reveals a 0 8cm in diameter  irregularly shaped  firm  tan lesion abutting an inked margin  A representative section is frozen as Frozen Section  1 and saved frozen  The lesion is too small for biochemical estrogen receptor study  The remainder is submitted entirely in B through E  Resident  George O  Kucyj  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LEFT   BIOPSY  CARCINOMA  PROBABLY INFILTRATING  AWAIT PERMANENTS   O R  Resident  Jo Ann E  Haney  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Gross.
