Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 MAY 95 ACCESSIONED ON  08 MAY 95 at 15 14 CLINICAL DATA  MGH  fine needle biopsy diagnosis carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  99    6 CM IN DIAMETER   POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 3  AND FOCAL INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  1    2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 8 OF 8 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Focal lymphatic invasion is identified  All resection margins are negative for carcinoma  the closest one is inferior and measures 0 5cm  LYMPH NODES  LEVEL ONE  RIGHT   LYMPHADENECTOMY  FIBROFATTY TISSUE  NO LYMPH NODES IDENTIFIED  SKIN  2 O CLOCK   BIOPSY  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITIES RECOGNIZED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  SKIN  4 O CLOCK   BIOPSY  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITIES RECOGNIZED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  SKIN  6 O CLOCK   BIOPSY  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITIES RECOGNIZED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  12 MAY 95 at 18 52                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 MAY 95 at 07 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are three separate specimens  Labeled  2 o clock   is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm ellipse of skin  excised to a depth of 0 5cm  entirely frozen as FX 1 and submitted in A  Labeled  4 o clock   is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm ellipse of skin  excised to a depth of 0 4cm  entirely frozen as FX 2 and submitted in B  Labeled  6 o clock   is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm ellipse of skin  excised to a depth of 0 4cm  entirely frozen as FX 3 and submitted in C   ADDON AJA  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 15 0cm  tan brown  overlying skin ellipse coating a 4 5cm in diameter areola and 1 5cm in diameter nipple  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm mass protrudes the skin surface 2 0cm lateral and slightly inferior to the nipple  The skin overlying this mass is dark brown to black in color  and is focally enfoliated  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm well circumscribed tan yel