D    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  68  to chromosome 17 signals  75  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  The results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Equivocal Amplification   Reference  Journal of Clinical Oncology 25 118 145   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 07   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 52 06PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Lymph Node  Right Axilla   Sentinel  749   Excision PART B  Breast  Right   Excision PART C  Breast  Right  Final Medial Margin   Excision PART D  Breast  Right  Final Superior Margin   Excision PART E  Breast  Right  Final Lateral Margin   Excision PART F  Breast  Right  Final inferior Margin   report_end  , Micro.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 MAY 95 ACCESSIONED ON  23 MAY 95 at 11 34 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT MASS   1 INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  40   APPROACHING TO WITHIN 1 MM OF INKED MARGIN AT ONE POINT  2 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  60   ABUTTING INKED MARGIN AT A FEW POINTS  3 FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  Intraductal carcinoma is present in the majority of the slides  The invasive foci form several nodules that range from REMOVED_DATE to 0 3cm  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D  Signed On  30 MAY 95 at 16 32 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 52 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm yellow fibrofatty breast lumpectomy specimen with an localizing needle and accompanying mammogram  Inked and sectioned to reveal a fatty cut surface with white rubbery fibrous bands  Representative sections are submitted in A through J  with areas of calcification in A through E  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  NO AREAS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA IDENTIFIED  O R  Resident  SCOTT D  URBAN  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Micro.
