inct masses or lesions grossly identified  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes W DD  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  non sentinel nodes  axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm aggregate of tan yellow lymph node bearing adipose tissue fragments  There are multiple lymph nodes dissected out ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  EE  5 whole lymph nodes  FF  4 whole lymph nodes  GG  2 whole lymph nodes  HH LL  1 bisected lymph node each  MM NN  Largest lymph node serially sectioned and entirely submitted  Gross Description by  JAMES BARRY Resident  TAI YUAN LIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  SENTINEL NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY   POSITIVE FOR CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  SENTINEL NODE  2  RIGHT AXILLARY   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE HALF  O R  Resident  JULIE ANN NAGLE  MD O R  Diagnosis by  SELIM NASSER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE PART B  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C  ADDITIONAL SUBAREOLAR TISSUE EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART D  SUBDERMAL NODULES  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART E  BREAST  RIGHT  SUPERIOR HALF OF CAVITY  FINAL SHAV PART F  BREAST  RIGHT  INFERIOR HALF OF CAVITY  FINAL SHAV PART G  RIGHT AXILLARY NON SENTINEL LYMPH NODES , Gross.
