Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 50 CLINICAL DATA  Microcalcifications      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  CORRECTED TISSUE SITE Revised by  Shane Meehan  MD Revised on 07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 55                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED GRADE REMOVED_DATE  75    PRESENT AT AN INKED MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBIFORM AND SOLID TYPE  25    WITH MICROCALCIFICATION  NOTE  No definite vascular invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Shane Meehan  MD Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 15                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 41     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm red and yellow  fibroadipose tissue fragment with a localizing needle and accompanying specimen radiograph  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm poorly defined  firm mass  with a tan cut surface  A portion of the mass is frozen as FX 1  saved frozen on Cox 5  The remainder the mass is submitted in A through C  with the rest of the specimen in D  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS  IN SITU AND INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Gross.
