y  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 09 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  left breast  is an unoriented breast biopsy measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  The superior margin is inked black  the inferior is inked blue  and the anterior surface is overinked green  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 1 0cm white firm  stellate area in the lateral half of the specimen  coming within 0 4cm from the closest resection margin  superior   Representative section of the stellate area is frozen as FX 1 and is resubmitted in cassette A  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes B J  Tumor is in B F  Lateral half in G and H  and medial half in I and J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast additional margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm irregular portion of breast tissue with a suture on one aspect marking the edge farthest from the tumor  The sutured half is black  th