f 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labelled with the patient name  unit number and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable nipple  Suture marking indicates superior  The specimen is inked black anteriorly and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm firm  yellow white mass with irregular borders that is located 0 2cm from the nearest deep margin  The mass is eccentrically located in the inferior external quadrant  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm soft  white yellow multilobulated lesion with bluish cystic spaces and solid areas are identified eccentrically in the lateral superior quadrant of the breast several centimeters from the main tumor  Representative tissue section through the tumor are included in cassette A G  Section C includes the nearest margin  Representative section through the second lesion are included through cassette H L  Section away from the tumor are included in M   N  The specimen also includes an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fibroadipose tissue containing lymph nodes  The lymph nodes are dissected and submitted through cassettes 0 R  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY , Micro.
