ior margin  2 5cm from the medial margin  and 2 8cm from the superior margin  The resection surfaces are entirely inked in black  and the area of the cavity is over inked in blue  Sectioning of the parenchyma reveals that the cavity is surrounded by irregular  white  fibrotic tissue  Additionally  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular  stellate  white lesion with central hemorrhage that is located laterally near the axial tail  and abuts the posterior margin and comes within 1 0cm of the anterior margin  SECTION CODE  A B  Cavity relative to anterior margin  C D  Representative sections of cavity  E   Fibrous rim around cavity relative to anterior margin  F   Closest medial margin  G   Closest superior margin  superior aspect over inked in green   H I  Representative sections of stellate  white lesion  relative to posterior margin  J   Closest anterior margin to stellate lesion  K M O  Lymph nodes from axillary tail  N   Representative section of nipple  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of yellow tan  fibroadipose tissue and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of yellow  fatty tissue  The larger fragment is bisected  and both pieces are entirely submitted in Cassette O  Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W P Andrew Lee  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   REGIONAL DISSECTION   report_end  , Micro.
