rozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are four specimens  Labeled  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 x 2 3cm specimen of fatty breast tissue with a short and a long stitch for orientation  The long stitch is designated lateral and the short superior  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1cm firm  circumscribed  whitish lesion with a 3mm margin of fat anteriorly  but abutting the posterior surface  covered only by a thin membrane  All other margins are widely free of tumor  Samples of tumor taken for the tissue bank and frozen for Cox 5  The red and green ink designates the anterior  blue and yellow the posterior aspect of the specimen  Representative sections of the tumor in relationship to the closest margins in A through D  Representative sections of normal appearing fatty breast parenchyma from the lateral and medial extremes of the specimens in E and F  Labeled  re excision medial half of biopsy cavity  including deep new margin  short superior  long new medial   is a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm oriented fibrofatty specimen  The posterior aspect is inked in black  The inner wall of the biopsy cavity is inked red  and the medial anterior aspects in green  Representative sections submitted in G J  Labeled  final shaved margin   is an aggregate of fibrofatty tissue measuring 4 x 4 x 1cm  Representative sections submitted in K N  Labeled  right axill